extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 79-81 (cache p080-p082, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. The entry heading Sham-Man O.C.C., a.k.a. the False Sorcerer, is on printed 79 below the end of the Road Sentinel; the nine numbered Powers of the Sham-Man/False Sorcerer O.C.C. are on printed 80 and run onto 81; the stat block is on printed 81 and ends above the Songjuicer heading. || HEADING: listed under Outback O.C.C.s on printed 56 as Sham-Man a.k.a. False Sorcerer O.C.C.; it is a practitioner of magic, so occ_group is magic. The class prints Base S.D.C. 4D6, stored as sdc_base, so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the Kwarla Mystic/Elder, Sham-Man/False Sorcerer ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 223, read off a render. Level 5 is printed 17,921-25,920. || P.P.E. (power 1): 2D4x10 plus P.E., +1D6+2 per level; the text layer prints 2D4xlO. || POWERS 2-6 are printed as references to the Ley Line Walker and Mystic abilities in the Rifts RPG (pages 83-85) with no text of their own; they are special_abilities entries that carry the reference. || SAVES (power 7): +2 vs Horror Factor, +1 vs possession and +2 vs ritual sorcery stored. || SPELLS (power 8): this book prints no spells; the class picks from the general invocations already in the catalog. 12 starting spells are stored as four starting groups (4 of level 1, 3 of level 2, 3 of level 3, 2 of level 4), and one spell per level from a level equal to his own as fourteen schedule entries each gated to its own spell level. Ritual sorcery at double P.P.E. and the fixed spell strength of 12 are prose in special_abilities and restrictions. || SPIRITUAL CHAMELEON (power 9): a percentage equal to the M.E. number +5% per level; an attribute-based chance, kept as a special_abilities entry. || SKILLS: Speaks English at 95% is stored as Language: Australian English at 95 with the catalog per-level rate. Dance or Musical Instrument is a choice between Dance and Play Musical Instrument. Lore: two of choice is a choice over the catalog Lore rows other than the two the class already grants. Hand to Hand: Basic with no others available is hand_to_hand costs of nothing. || RELATED: Electrical and Mechanical Basic only are Basic Electronics and Basic Mechanics. Wilderness Survival is printed under Espionage and is reached through the Wilderness category. Pilot except Robot Elite, Power Armor and military vehicles is stored as the Robot Combat rows, Robots & Power Armor and the five Military rows. Cowboy, Military and Rogue are printed None and left out. || MONEY: 2D6x100 in cash stored; the 3D6x100 in saleable items is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: wristwatch and the clothing accessories have no row; the canteen is printed twice in the list and stored once; the optional items (staff or walking stick, binoculars, laser distancer, air filter, tinted goggles, cape or cloak, Aboriginal items) are at the G.M.''s word and are in GM Notes. The sidearm choice offers this book''s pistols and the armor choice its nonmetallic homespun rows."
---

## Lore

When magic came back to Australia, the Aboriginal tribes regained an old
inheritance. A few outsiders felt the same pull without any tie of ancestry
to the land. They took themselves for shamans at first; what they turned out
to practise is a looser kind of sorcery, drawn from the land and its spirits
but weaker than most traditions and easier to misuse.

Nobody trusts them much. Outback settlers are wary of any magic, and the
tribes regard the "sham-man" as a pretender who imitates what he has no
right to, tolerating rather than welcoming him. Some Sham-Men earn the name
as tricksters and exploiters. Others study Aboriginal culture in earnest,
hoping one day to work magic as a true shaman does. Most simply ignore the
stigma and use what they have, for healing or for war.

## GM Notes

Spell strength never improves: targets always need 12 or higher to save.
Ritual sorcery costs double the P.P.E.

Spiritual Chameleon: percentage equal to the M.E. attribute number, +5% per
level of experience. On a failure the spirit, demon or Millennium being sees
through the pose and may be offended; a Millennium Tree or the Great Reef
tends to teleport the Sham-Man away or call up a storm.

Powers 2 to 6 are the Ley Line Walker''s Sense Ley Line and Magic Energy,
Read Ley Lines, Ley Line Drifting and Ley Line Rejuvenation, and the
Mystic''s Sense Supernatural Evil, used as printed in the main Rifts rules.

Optional starting items, G.M. has the final word: a wood or metal staff or
walking stick, binoculars, laser distancer, air filter, tinted goggles, cape
or cloak, and Aboriginal items of importance such as bones, bark scratchings
or a notebook of copied cave paintings. The sidearm comes with two reloads.

Money is 2D6x100 in cash plus 3D6x100 in saleable items. Australian dollars
equal credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sham-man');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sham-man';

